# Testing Rule: Never Mock LLM

- [CRITICAL][!NO-MOCKS] Do NOT mock, stub, fake, or otherwise simulate the LLM in any test (unit, integration, feature, system, smoke).
- [CRITICAL][!REAL-LLM] All tests must call the real LLM endpoint. If the LLM is unavailable, skip or fail explicitly rather than mocking.
- [CRITICAL][!NO-SYNTHETIC] Do NOT inject canned tool_call payloads or synthetic LLM responses in tests.
- [CRITICAL][!ALL-SCOPES] Apply this rule across all scopes (backend, frontend/system, integration, CI/local).

- [EXECUTE][!NO-CONFIRM] Default to execute: run all needed commands/tests/fixes end-to-end without asking for confirmation.
- [BLOCK-ONLY-IF][!PAUSE] Pause only if an action is destructive (data loss), needs missing credentials, or requirements conflict.
- [RESILIENT][!RETRY] If blocked (e.g., endpoint down, missing key), try safe mitigations (retries/backoff) once; otherwise report the block with what was tried.
- [TESTS][!FULL-SUITE] For tests, always run the relevant suite (or full suite if unspecified) after changes; rerun after fixes.